  <section class="tp-section" aria-labelledby="thumb-what-headline">
    <div class="tp-section-inner">
      <div class="tp-section-head">
        <span class="tp-eyebrow text-caption-mono">The basics</span>
        <h2 id="thumb-what-headline" class="tp-section-title">What a TikTok thumbnail actually is</h2>
        <p class="tp-section-sub">
          A TikTok thumbnail is the cover image attached to a video post. It is not a random video frame.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="tp-prose">
        <p>
          When a creator uploads to TikTok, the platform lets them choose a cover from the video timeline.
          That image is stored separately from the MP4, then resized for the feed, the profile grid, search
