        <span class="tp-eyebrow text-caption-mono">Troubleshooting</span>
        <h2 id="thumb-problems-headline" class="tp-section-title">When a TikTok thumbnail will not load</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="tp-prose">
        <p>
          Most failures come from the post, not the downloader. A private account, a friends-only video, a
          deleted post, or a region-restricted upload will not return public cover metadata. If the page
          returns a clear error, check that the link opens in a logged-out browser. If TikTok asks you to log
          in, no public downloader can reach the cover.
        </p>
        <p>
          A second common issue is an expired share link. TikTok short links can resolve to the wrong place
          after the post is removed. Open the short link once, copy the final URL from the address bar, and
          paste that full URL into the form. The same trick fixes links that were copied from a chat app and
          picked up extra tracking parameters.
        </p>
        <p>
          If the preview appears but the download does not start, your browser may be blocking the file. Check
          the download permissions for the site, disable a download manager temporarily, or try another
          browser. On iOS, a focus mode or content blocker can also interrupt a download. The image still
          exists at the source; the browser is simply refusing to save it.
        </p>
        <p>
